        "accounting_document_item": "Preserve the FI item value returned by the authoritative FI source in the projection. When joining MHND/MHNK history to FI items, numeric item keys such as 1 and 001 are SAP-equivalent after leading-zero normalization; this normalization is relationship-only and must not rewrite the displayed FI key.",
        "ledger": "Read the unique leading ledger from live API_LEDGER_SRV/A_Ledger. Operational account-item Cube may project a blank Ledger; do not filter it by a guessed ledger and drop items. Verify the operational item's leading-ledger relationship with independent FI evidence before assigning the resolved ledger; otherwise leave unknown.",
        "dunning_as_of_status": "For as_of equal to business_date, use DunningLevel and LastDunningDate on the FI item, not A_CustomerDunning as a historical item snapshot: confirmed_current when level is nonzero and date is present, otherwise not_dunned when those fields were actually read completely. For historical dates use the approved dunning-history Skill events: an exactly related, provably ordered event is confirmed_before_cutoff even when its dunning_level is 0; level 0 must be preserved and is not the same as absence of an event. Use not_dunned only when the complete historical event scope contains no related event, and unknown only when that evidence is unavailable or ambiguous. The required historical_dunning_master_snapshot_not_available limitation is a scope disclosure, not an evidence gap and must not lower source_complete, evidence_complete or business_complete.",
        "last_dunning_date": "Current item LastDunningDate, or the last provably ordered historical event. Null when no event is established, never inferred from current customer master data.",
        "aging_bucket": "Compare NetDueDate (or DueCalculationBaseDate if NetDueDate is absent) with as_of: not_due, 1_30, 31_60, 61_90, over_90, unknown. Preserve each item's amount and currency; never net credits or special G/L against ordinary trade overdue amounts.",
