        ,"action_required": "True only for items that require an evidenced follow-up action. Not-yet-due ordinary debit receivables use monitor_until_due and remain outside the action worklist."
        ,"action_code": "Deterministic action classification in this order: evidence gap, dunning block, special G/L, credit balance, overdue follow-up, monitor until due."
        ,"action_priority": "SAPBusinessAgents processing priority, never SAP native dunning priority: high for evidence gaps, blocks, or over 90 days; medium for 31-90 days, special G/L, or credits; low for 1-30 days; none for monitor-only items."
      },
      "businessStatusDefinition": "Classify each requested customer independently: incomplete evidence=inconclusive; otherwise any deterministic action other than resolve_evidence_gap or monitor_until_due=attention; otherwise normal. Every canonical item receives action_required, action_code and SAPBusinessAgents action_priority. Not-yet-due ordinary debit items remain visible but do not enter the action worklist. Record business_status inherits its customer status. Aggregate inconclusive before attention before normal. Current customer dunning master only supplies procedure/block/recipient/responsible person; do not substitute it for item dunning level/date. For a historical run, historical_dunning_master_snapshot_not_available is a required non-blocking scope limitation and is not incomplete evidence.",
